-- title:
--   Common chart, exceptional stability and valuative cover at the ends
-- statement:
--   **Base data.** Fix primes $q$ and $\ell$ with $q\ge 5$, $\ell\ge 3$, $\ell\ne q$, and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ and $\xi\in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity; the hypothesis `hι` requires a ring homomorphism $\iota\colon L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota(\xi)=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq\operatorname{LaurentSeries}L$, and let `hK` require $K=\,$[`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((t))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_H$ of level $(q\ell)^2M'$, where $H=\ker\big((\mathbb Z/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times\big)$ is the group of units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation ring (a domain) with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, with $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ (`hAq`) and with $\xi$ in the image of $A$ (`hξA`), and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular $j$-function under the coefficientwise map $\mathbb Q\to L$ (`hj`). Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak m_A$ (`hϖ`), and let $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   Write $C=\,$`chartAlgFin A ↥K j` for the integral closure of $A[j]$ in $K$, and $\mathfrak X=\,$[`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) for the two-chart integral model, the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec}C\leftarrow X_{\mathrm{Mid}}\to\operatorname{Spec}C'$ with $C'$ the integral closure of $A[j^{-1}]$, together with its structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec}A$. Let $y\subset C$ be a maximal ideal containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hy`, `hϖy`) which is supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi\colon C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of elements $j_0\in\Omega$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j_0$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   **The Drinfeld-chart hypothesis `hArig`.** This hypothesis asserts, at every point $z$ of $\mathfrak X$ such that the germ at $z$ of the global section of $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X}$ determined by $\varpi$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and for every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec}C$ with image $z$ under the chart morphism `ιFin` whose prime is supersingular in the sense just described, the existence of a coefficient ring and a chart presentation with the seven properties (a)–(g) listed below: a complete discrete valuation ring $W_\ast$ (a domain), a homomorphism $\sigma\colon A\to W_\ast$ with $\mathfrak m_{W_\ast}=(\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W_\ast[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f-(X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1)\in(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion of the stalk $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$ onto $W_\ast[[X_0,X_1]]/\big(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1})v-fu\big)$.
--
--   **The fixed point and the fixed chart witness.** Fixed are: a point $z$ of $\mathfrak X$, the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ at $z$ (`hϖz`) lying in the maximal ideal of the stalk (`hz`), a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec}C$ with `ιFin`-image $z$ (`hy'`) satisfying the supersingularity condition (`hss'`) and with $y'=y$ (`hy'y`); and one witness as above: a complete discrete valuation ring $W_1$, $\sigma_1\colon A\to W_1$ with $\mathfrak m_{W_1}=(\sigma_1\varpi)$, power series $f_1,u_1,v_1$ with $u_1,v_1$ units (`hu₁`, `hv₁`) and $f_1-(X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1)\in(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (`hf₁`), and an isomorphism $e_1$ from the completion of $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$ onto $S=W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/\big(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1})v_1-f_1u_1\big)$. Writing $\mathrm{toC}$ for the map from the stalk to its completion, $\mathrm{mkS}$ for the quotient map onto $S$, and $\mathrm{germY}$ for the canonical map $C\to\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$ through the chart `ιFin`, the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts the seven clauses:
--
--   (a) for $a\in A$, $e_1$ carries the image in the completion of the germ at $z$ of $a$ to the class of the constant $\sigma_1(a)$;
--
--   (b) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $L$-automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ which is a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ in the sense of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) (for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f,g$ of level $\Gamma_H((q\ell)^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions, $g$'s expansion nonzero, and all $x\in K$ with Laurent expansion $f/g$, the complex expansion of $\tau x$ times the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k\mathrm{conjElemN}(q\ell,\gamma^{-1})$ equals that of $f\mid_k\mathrm{conjElemN}(q\ell,\gamma^{-1})$, for any $\iota$ normalising $\xi$), the subalgebra $C$ is $\tau$-stable;
--
--   (c) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\cap\Gamma(\ell)$ and such $\tau$ preserving $C$, the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$ is congruent to the identity modulo $y'$;
--
--   (d) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and such $\tau$ preserving $C$ and congruent to the identity modulo $y'$ on $C$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c\in W_1$ and a matrix $M\in M_2(W_1)$ with: $\theta$ computes the action of $\tau|_C$ on $S$ through $e_1\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}$; $\theta$ fixes the classes of constants; $\theta(X_{j})-\sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ lies in the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0,X_1$; $c^{q+1}\equiv1$, $M_{ij}\equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_{W_1}$; $c\equiv 1$ if $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$; and $c\not\equiv1$ if $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity;
--
--   (e) branch separation: for integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and primes $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, each not containing both classes of $X_0,X_1$, each containing the class of $\sigma_1\varpi$, and each containing an element $a_iX_0+b_iX_1+h$ with $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ along $e_1\circ\mathrm{toC}$ are distinct;
--
--   (f) for such a prime $P$ containing an element $1\cdot X_0+0\cdot X_1+h$ with $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, and for $a\in C$: the image of $a$ in the completion lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e_1$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$;
--
--   (g) a Hasse-type clause: [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (the expansion `jqModC L` of $j$ with all exponents multiplied by $q\ell$) lies in $K$ and in $C$; there is $a_0\in A$ with the difference of this element and $a_0$ in $y'$; and there are $e_0\ge1$ and $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that for all $a,b\in W_1$ with at least one of them a unit and $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_{W_1}$ the value $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0}h_{(i,e_0-i)}a^ib^{e_0-i}$ of the degree-$e_0$ part of $h$ is a unit, while $e_1$ carries the image in the completion of that difference to the class of $h$.
--
--   **The centre, the blow-up algebra and the exceptional valuation.** Let $J\subseteq C$ be an ideal with `hJ`: $J$ is the infimum of the ideals obtained as follows — for $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$, pull back along $\tau|_C$ the contraction along $e_1\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}$ of the ideal of $S$ generated by the classes of $\sigma_1\varpi_t$, $X_0$ and $X_1$. Let $B$ be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ with `hB`: $B=C\big[\{x\in K:\ x\varpi_t\in J\}\big]$. Let $W$ be a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`). Four further hypothesis groups are imposed: `hR1`, that $C\subseteq B$ and every element of $K$ is a quotient of two elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator; `hR2`, that $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$ and that $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses), that an element of $L$ lies in $W$ exactly when it comes from $A$, that $\mathfrak m_W$ is generated by $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that an element of $C$ lies in $y$ exactly when it lies in $\mathfrak m_W$, and that $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak m_W$; and `hEQ` (five clauses), that (i) for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho\colon B\to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of $k[X_0,X_1]$ by the ideal generated by `drinfeldPoly q k - 1`) with kernel the elements of $\mathfrak m_W$, compatible with $A\to k$, and such that each level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W$ acts through [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325) by a pair $(\mathrm{redQ}_q(\gamma),c)$ with $c\in\mathbb F_{q^2}^\times$ in the kernel of $(g,c)\mapsto\det(g)\,c^{q+1}$, with $c\ne1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\ne\mathrm{id}$; (ii) $B$ is stable under all such $\tau$ for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; (iii) every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ contains the $\tau$-image of every element of $\mathfrak m_W\cap B$ for some $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and associated $\tau$; (iv) an element of $B$ all of whose translates under such $\gamma,\tau$ lie in $\mathfrak m_W$ is divisible by $\varpi$ in $B$; (v) a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ which preserves $y$ on $C$ preserves $W$.
--
--   **The ends.** Let `ends` be a finite set of subrings of $K$ with `hends`: a subring $O$ belongs to it if and only if there is $a\in J$, nonzero in $K$, and a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a=C\big[\{x\in K:\ xa\in J\}\big]$, such that $O$ is the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$ (an element of $K$ lies in $O$ exactly when it is $g/h$ with $g,h\in B_a$, $h\notin P$), every element of $y$ that lies in $O$ is a non-unit of $O$, and $B\not\subseteq O$. Finally `hperm` requires that for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $W$, each $O\in$ `ends` has some $O'\in$ `ends` with $f\in O\iff\tau f\in O'$ for all $f\in K$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Three assertions hold.
--
--   First, a common chart at the ends: there exists an $A$-subalgebra $B_c$ of $K$ which is of finite type over $A$, is stable under every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, and is such that for every $O\in$ `ends` one has $B_c\subseteq O$ and $O$ is the corresponding localisation: an element $f\in K$ lies in $O$ if and only if there are $g,h\in B_c$ with $h$ a unit of $O$ whenever $h\in O$, and $fh=g$.
--
--   Second, stability of the exceptional valuation: for every $O\in$ `ends`, every $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$, if $\tau$ maps $O$ into $W$ then $W$ is $\tau$-stable, i.e. $f\in W\iff\tau f\in W$ for all $f\in K$.
--
--   Third, a valuative cover: for every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ such that an element of $L$ lies in $V$ exactly when it comes from $A$, such that $C\subseteq V$, and such that every element of $y$ lies in $\mathfrak m_V$, either $B\subseteq V$, or there is $O\in$ `ends` with $O\subseteq V$ and with every non-unit of $O$ lying in $\mathfrak m_V$.
--
--   This is the global geometric step in the study of the ends of the blow-up of the supersingular chart of the two-chart integral model of the modular function field $K$ at level $(q\ell)^2M'$: the ends are shown to be localisations of a single finite-type, equivariant affine chart, the exceptional valuation $W$ to be stable whenever an end is carried into it, and the valuations of $K$ lying over the supersingular point $y$ to be covered by $B$ together with the ends. It is obtained by combining `exists_commonChart_ends_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked`, `exceptionalValuation_stable_of_end_le_translate_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked` and `valuativeCover_ends_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked`, and feeds the cyclic-decomposition assembly at this level.
